#
# Dockerfile-specific ignore file for `Dockerfile.plane-jobs`. BuildKit looks
# for `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile and uses it instead of
# the context's `.dockerignore`, so the repository root can be the build context
# (the Rust binary embeds one `apps/api` template, see the Dockerfile) without
# uploading `apps/server/target/` (tens of gigabytes) or the Django virtualenv.
#
# Patterns are matched against the context root; a `*` does not cross `/`.

# Everything at the top level is out (other apps, packages, .git, ...).
*
!apps

# The Rust workspace is in.
!apps/server
# ... but not its build output, local dev stack, generated scenarios or the
# separate testkit workspace (never a dependency of the server binaries).
apps/server/target
apps/server/dev
apps/server/scenarios
apps/server/tools
apps/server/deploy
apps/server/docs
apps/server/*.md
apps/server/crates/plane-testkit

# Django is out except for the single template `csrf.rs` embeds.
apps/api/*
!apps/api/templates
